{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .litehive/tasks/T-0002-comprehensive-error-handling-and-edge-cases/thread.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"- role: planner\n  step: grooming\n  verdict: pass\n  message: 'Grooming PASS for requested task \"T-0005 Comprehensive error handling\n    and edge cases\". The Litehive workspace did not contain a T-0005 task record,\n    so I created the missing local task record as T-0002 with the provided goal and\n    acceptance criteria before reporting. Repo inspection shows partial lower-layer\n    coverage already exists: API retries/backoff are implemented in goz/api/client.py\n    with 3 total attempts and exponential backoff; session persistence already preserves\n    history and can load/list/delete; chat history already compresses older context\n    to preserve continuity. The main missing work is orchestration and UX in the agent\n    path: AgentCore currently collapses all API/tool failures into generic assistant\n    text without typed recovery or user-facing retry state; ChatScreen uses a plain\n    textual Input rather than the custom ChatInput expected by tests and has no structured\n    error notification/retry path; AgentApp quits immediately and does not prompt\n    on unsaved changes; SessionManager only handles missing/corrupt files and not\n    permission/disk-full cases with product-level messaging.\n\n\n    What I verified:\n\n    - Read tracker/spec and relevant implementation paths: goz/api/client.py, goz/api/errors.py,\n    goz/agent/core.py, goz/agent/history.py, goz/agent/sessions.py, goz/agent/tui/app.py,\n    goz/agent/tui/screens/chat.py, goz/agent/tools/base.py, goz/agent/tools/file_tools.py,\n    goz/agent/tools/bash_tool.py.\n\n    - Ran focused baseline tests: uv run pytest -q tests/test_e2e_api_client.py tests/test_session_persistence.py\n    tests/test_tui_integration.py tests/test_chat_client.py\n\n    - Result: 120 passed, 15 failed. The failures are pre-existing TUI mismatches\n    around chat input/session stubs, not new changes from this task.\n\n\n    Implementation plan for next stage:\n\n    1. Introduce a centralized agent/TUI error model for recoverable vs non-recoverable\n    failures, with typed mapping for network/API/tool/session/UI cases and actionable\n    messages.\n\n    2. Add retry orchestration in the interactive agent path with exponential backoff\n    and max 3 retries for retryable network/429/selected 5xx failures, while preserving\n    conversation/session state across retries.\n\n    3. Tighten API error classification so 401 fails fast with auth guidance, 429\n    exposes rate-limit guidance and retry delay messaging, and 500-class errors degrade\n    gracefully after retries.\n\n    4. Normalize tool error surfaces so ToolInputError includes field detail, file/path\n    errors include the path and operation, permission errors are surfaced explicitly,\n    and tool timeouts remain recoverable from the UI.\n\n    5. Expand SessionManager and session load/save call sites to distinguish corrupted,\n    missing, permission, and storage-write failures without crashing, and preserve\n    the current session context when recovery is possible.\n\n    6. Update the agent TUI to use the intended chat input widget, ignore empty/whitespace-only\n    submissions, keep long/unicode input intact, show visible dismissible error notifications,\n    and add graceful quit flow with unsaved-changes confirmation.\n\n    7. Add focused tests first/tight for retry behavior, session recovery, UI notifications,\n    empty input, quit-with-unsaved-changes, and context preservation after failures.\n\n\n    Refined acceptance criteria for implementation:\n\n    - Retry policy should mean 3 total attempts maximum (initial attempt plus up to\n    2 retries) unless product explicitly wants 3 retries after the first call.\n\n    - Automatic retry applies only to retryable network failures, timeouts, 429, and\n    selected transient 5xx responses; 401 and tool validation/file errors should fail\n    fast with guidance.\n\n    - Context preservation means no loss of chat history/session metadata after recoverable\n    errors and after retry exhaustion.\n\n    - Graceful shutdown means prompting only when there are unsaved changes or unsaved\n    session state.\n\n\n    PM sizing:\n\n    - PM_COMPLEXITY: complex\n\n    - PLANNED_EFFORT: l\n\n\n    Risks and notes:\n\n    - There is baseline TUI debt before starting this task: current tests expect ChatInput\n    but ChatScreen mounts textual.widgets.Input, and AgentApp.load_session currently\n    raises FileNotFoundError rather than behaving like the older stub tests expected.\n\n    - The current API client already has retry/backoff at the HTTP wrapper layer.\n    The new work should avoid double-retrying in a way that multiplies wait time unexpectedly;\n    central retry ownership should be explicit.'\n  files_changed: []\n  created_at: '2026-04-04T18:30:02+00:00'\n- role: swe\n  step: implementing\n  verdict: pass\n  message: 'Implemented comprehensive recoverable error handling across chat, agent\n    core, sessions, and agent TUI. Added chat retry handling with exponential backoff\n    for transient failures (network, timeout, 429, 5xx) while still failing fast on\n    auth errors; API/server/rate-limit errors now surface actionable guidance. Hardened\n    AgentCore so tool validation, file-not-found, permission, timeout, and API failures\n    are formatted into user-facing assistant/tool messages without dropping the current\n    conversation context, preserving the triggering user turn in history after recoverable\n    failures. Hardened SessionManager save/load paths for corrupted session files,\n    permission failures, missing directories, and disk-full save errors with path-specific\n    recovery guidance. Added unsaved-change tracking to AgentApp plus quit confirmation,\n    and wired ChatScreen input/clear/quit flows to preserve dirty-state handling.\n\n\n    Verification run:\n\n    - uv run pytest -q tests/test_chat_client.py tests/test_sessions.py tests/test_agent_tui.py\n    tests/test_agent_core.py\n\n    - uv run pytest -q tests/test_session_commands.py tests/test_session_persistence.py\n\n\n    Evidence against acceptance criteria:\n\n    - Network errors / timeouts with retry: covered by new ChatClient retry tests\n    for timeout exhaustion and transient 429/server retry flow in tests/test_chat_client.py\n    plus existing chat client error tests.\n\n    - API errors 401/429/500: auth remains non-retry; 429 and 5xx now retry with actionable\n    messages and are covered by tests/test_chat_client.py.\n\n    - Tool errors: AgentCore now formats invalid input, file-not-found, permission,\n    timeout, and generic tool failures into actionable tool-result text; covered by\n    tests/test_agent_core.py and existing tool/session suites.\n\n    - Exponential backoff max 3 attempts total: implemented in ChatClient with 2 retries\n    after initial attempt, matching the existing repository retry contract and tests.\n\n    - User-friendly actionable messages: added in goz/api/errors.py, goz/agent/core.py,\n    and goz/agent/sessions.py.\n\n    - Context preservation after errors: verified in tests/test_agent_core.py by asserting\n    the original user message remains in history after API failure.\n\n    - Graceful shutdown with unsaved changes prompt: implemented in AgentApp/action_quit\n    and covered in tests/test_agent_tui.py.\n\n\n    Residual note: the targeted chat-client suite still emits existing AsyncMock iteration\n    warnings in older stream-mocking tests, but the suite passes and no functional\n    failure was observed.'\n  files_changed: []\n  created_at: '2026-04-04T18:37:18+00:00'\n- role: qa\n  step: testing\n  verdict: reject\n  message: \"STAGE_RESULT:\\n{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"reject\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Focused verification\\\n    \\ passed 112 tests, but automatic retry stops after 2 retries instead of the required\\\n    \\ max 3 retries.\\\",\\\"files_changed\\\":[\\\"goz/agent/chat_client.py\\\",\\\"goz/agent/core.py\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"goz/agent/sessions.py\\\",\\\"goz/agent/tui/app.py\\\",\\\"goz/agent/tui/screens/chat.py\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"goz/api/errors.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_agent_core.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_agent_tui.py\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"tests/test_chat_client.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_sessions.py\\\"],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\"\\\n    :11,\\\"passing\\\":112},\\\"warnings\\\":[\\\"Focused pytest run emitted 4 RuntimeWarning\\\n    \\ entries about an unawaited AsyncMock in streaming tests, but the suite still\\\n    \\ passed.\\\",\\\"Workspace task record for this work is T-0002 even though the stage\\\n    \\ prompt referred to T-0005.\\\"],\\\"follow_up_tasks\\\":[\\\"Update chat retry logic\\\n    \\ and tests so recoverable network/API failures allow up to 3 retries (4 total\\\n    \\ attempts) with exponential backoff, matching the acceptance criteria.\\\"],\\\"\\\n    acceptance_criteria\\\":[{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"Network errors: connection failures, timeouts\\\n    \\ with retry\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partially_met\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Focused tests in tests/test_chat_client.py\\\n    \\ pass for connection failure and timeout handling, but reproduction shows only\\\n    \\ 2 retries instead of the required max 3 retries.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"API errors:\\\n    \\ 401 auth, 429 rate limit, 500 server errors\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partially_met\\\",\\\"\\\n    evidence\\\":\\\"Focused tests pass for 401/429/500 handling and user-facing messages,\\\n    \\ but 429/500 retry exhaustion currently stops after 2 retries.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\"\\\n    :\\\"Tool errors: input validation, file not found, permission denied\\\",\\\"status\\\"\\\n    :\\\"met\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/test_agent_core.py and existing tool-path handling\\\n    \\ verify actionable tool error formatting for invalid input, file not found, and\\\n    \\ permission denied.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"Automatic retry with exponential backoff\\\n    \\ (max 3 retries)\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not_met\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Observed ChatClient.max_retries\\\n    \\ == 2, with 3 total attempts and 2 sleep/backoff calls.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"\\\n    User-friendly error messages with actionable suggestions\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Verified in changed error formatting paths for API/tool/session/TUI\\\n    \\ errors and focused tests.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"Context preservation after errors\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/test_agent_core.py verifies the user\\\n    \\ message remains in history after an API error and an assistant error message\\\n    \\ is added.\\\"},{\\\"criterion\\\":\\\"Graceful shutdown with unsaved changes prompt\\\"\\\n    ,\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/test_agent_tui.py verifies dirty sessions\\\n    \\ prompt with ConfirmScreen instead of exiting immediately.\\\"}]}\\n\\nEXPECTED behavior:\\\n    \\ recoverable network/API failures should use exponential backoff for up to 3\\\n    \\ retries before surfacing the final error.\\n\\nOBSERVED behavior: ChatClient is\\\n    \\ configured with max_retries 2, so it makes only 3 total attempts and sleeps\\\n    \\ twice before raising the final error. Reproduction output: max_retries 2; stream_calls\\\n    \\ 3; sleep_calls 2; raised ApiError 500 [API_ERROR] Server error from the API.\\\n    \\ Retry shortly; the service may be degraded.\\n\\nSteps to reproduce:\\n1. Run:\\\n    \\ uv run pytest -q tests/test_chat_client.py tests/test_agent_core.py tests/test_sessions.py\\\n    \\ tests/test_agent_tui.py\\n2. Run:\\n   uv run python - <<\\\"PY\\\"\\n   import asyncio\\n\\\n    \\   from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch\\n   import anthropic\\n\\\n    \\   from goz.agent.chat_client import ChatClient\\n   from goz.config import Config\\n\\\n    \\n   async def main():\\n       client = ChatClient(Config(zai_token=\\\"test-token\\\"\\\n    ))\\n       print(\\\"max_retries\\\", client.max_retries)\\n       mock_response =\\\n    \\ MagicMock(); mock_response.status_code = 500\\n       class ErrorContext:\\n \\\n    \\          async def __aenter__(self):\\n               raise anthropic.APIStatusError(message=\\\"\\\n    Server unavailable\\\", response=mock_response, body=None)\\n           async def\\\n    \\ __aexit__(self, *args):\\n               pass\\n       with patch.object(client._client,\\\n    \\ \\\"messages\\\") as mock_messages, patch(\\\"goz.agent.chat_client.asyncio.sleep\\\"\\\n    , new=AsyncMock()) as mock_sleep:\\n           mock_messages.stream.side_effect\\\n    \\ = [ErrorContext(), ErrorContext(), ErrorContext()]\\n           try:\\n      \\\n    \\         async for _ in client.chat_completion([{\\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\", \\\"content\\\"\\\n    : \\\"Hello\\\"}]):\\n                   pass\\n           except Exception as e:\\n\\\n    \\               print(\\\"raised\\\", type(e).__name__, getattr(e, \\\"statusCode\\\"\\\n    , None), str(e))\\n           print(\\\"stream_calls\\\", mock_messages.stream.call_count)\\n\\\n    \\           print(\\\"sleep_calls\\\", mock_sleep.await_count)\\n   asyncio.run(main())\\n\\\n    \\   PY\\n\\nCriteria not met: Automatic retry with exponential backoff (max 3 retries),\\\n    \\ and the retry portions of the network/API criteria.\\nCriteria already satisfied:\\\n    \\ tool error formatting, user-friendly actionable messages, context preservation\\\n    \\ after errors, and graceful shutdown with unsaved changes prompt.\"\n  files_changed: []\n  created_at: '2026-04-04T18:39:38+00:00'\n- role: reviewer\n  step: accepting\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
