{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'litehive --help'","aggregated_output":"usage: litehive [-h]\n                {configure,status,queue,repair,tasks,web,daemon,add,intake,run,dirty-worktree-gate,rollback,recover,move,prioritize,promote,requeue,resume,abandon,stop,close,update,report}\n                ...\n\npositional arguments:\n  {configure,status,queue,repair,tasks,web,daemon,add,intake,run,dirty-worktree-gate,rollback,recover,move,prioritize,promote,requeue,resume,abandon,stop,close,update,report}\n    configure           Initialize litehive workspace config\n    status              Show workspace status\n    queue               Show the active task and queued order\n    repair              Repair stale active tasks, interrupted runs, and queue\n                        inconsistencies\n    tasks               Open the task view\n    web                 Serve the local queue and session monitor\n    daemon              Manage the Litehive pool daemon\n    add                 Create a queued task\n    intake              Create a rough task from a freeform brain dump using\n                        an LLM\n    run                 Run the next task once\n    dirty-worktree-gate\n                        Report whether dirty git state should block the\n                        workspace and explain ownership\n    rollback            Revert a task checkpoint commit and requeue the task\n    recover             Requeue a completed task without reverting code\n    move                Move a queued task to a 1-based position\n    prioritize          Move multiple queued tasks to the front in the\n                        requested order\n    promote             Move a queued task to the front of the queue\n    requeue             Requeue a flagged or closed task\n    resume              Resume an interrupted, flagged, or closed task from\n                        its current stage\n    abandon             Cancel a flagged or closed task and remove it from the\n                        queue\n    stop                Stop the current active task cleanly\n    close               Close a task with an explicit non-implementation\n                        outcome (wont_do, deferred, duplicate)\n    update              Update task engine and metadata\n    report              Submit a stage verdict for the active task\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
